{"ts":"2026-11-23T04:43:26.110290549Z","author":"scourge-security","event":"CommentAdded","data":{"comment_id":"th-22lajf.1","thread_id":"th-22lajf","body":"risk:medium — A detached proxy can be orphaned on the start failure path. `started` becomes true only after `teapot_json` returns and its JSON parse succeeds. If `proxy start --detach` launches the proxy but the CLI then times out, is interrupted, or emits malformed JSON, control reaches `finally` with `started=False`; `cleanup_run` skips `proxy stop`, removes the run root (including the control socket), and raises. That can leave a live no-enforce proxy holding the attached approval with its normal control path deleted. Record that start was attempted before dispatch, then probe/stop after every start attempt and remove the root only after verified termination; add a regression test where the start call launches and then raises or returns invalid JSON."}}
{"ts":"2026-11-23T04:43:26.832285413Z","author":"scourge-security","event":"ReviewerVoted","data":{"review_id":"cr-2etlqi","vote":"block","reason":"Unresolved risk:medium orphaned-proxy cleanup path in capture_fresh_pair.py: a detached proxy that starts before the CLI errors is not stopped and can lose its control socket.","target_commit":"e2bcc9597d049e006745cdc23f9b132086c0a59b"}}
{"ts":"2026-11-23T04:47:23.107234484Z","author":"outcome-contract","event":"CommentAdded","data":{"comment_id":"th-22lajf.2","thread_id":"th-22lajf","body":"Fixed: start_attempted is set before dispatch; cleanup stops and then verifies proxy status running=false after every attempted start, only removes the run root after that verification, and remains nonzero on stop/status/removal failure. Added an exact launch-then-response-failure regression plus stop/removal failure tests, and regenerated twin evidence with post-stop status commands."}}
